========================================================================
CRYPTO GATE HONESTY (do not greenwash)
========================================================================

Reference: `openOODA/bootstrap/STDLIB_CRYPTO_MATH.oot` — claims 8 product
crypto surfaces are **gate-only** via `process_exit(1)` (math not audited).

Live re-measure of the listed eight:

| File | Lines | `process_exit` | Gate status |
|------|------:|---------------:|-------------|
| `sec/crypto/ed25519_ops.oo` | 302 | 18 | **GATED** (load-bearing) |
| `sec/crypto/dilithium_ops.oo` | 281 | 12 | **GATED** |
| `sec/crypto/double_ratchet_ops.oo` | 272 | 18 | **GATED** |
| `sec/crypto/groth16_ops.oo` | 233 | 11 | **GATED** |
| `sec/crypto/kyber.oo` | 437 | 9 | **PARTIAL gate** (types/helpers may run; ops pe) |
| `sec/crypto/falcon_ops.oo` | 144 | **0** | **DRIFT — no process_exit** |
| `sec/crypto/secp256k1_ops.oo` | 239 | **0** | **DRIFT — no process_exit** |
| `sec/crypto/plonk_ops.oo` | 181 | **0** | **DRIFT — no process_exit** |

Honesty:

1. **Do not claim** "all std crypto math is fail-closed gated." Three listed
   `_ops` bodies currently expose synthetic/partial arithmetic without
   `process_exit(1)`.
2. Presence of large line counts + type surface **≠** audited crypto.
   STDLIB residual still applies: math not audited; no CT claim.
3. `zkstark_engine.oo` (314, pe=0) and monofiles `hmac`/`sphincs`/`aes_gcm_siv`
   are **outside** the STDLIB-8 table but look "real" by structure — still
   residual / not production-proven.
4. Recommended DE fix (agy, not this pass): either restore `process_exit(1)`
   on every public crypto math entry for falcon/secp256k1/plonk, **or** update
   `STDLIB_CRYPTO_MATH.oot` with an honest "partial synthetic / ungated"
   class. Prefer restore gate until math audit lands.

Related monofiles outside STDLIB-8 that still use pe for fail-closed:
  hmac (8), sphincs (12), aes_gcm_siv (6), sign (4) — partial coverage only.

